  "name": "AsDecimalKeepsDecimal",
  "comment": "Stage 4 (ruling 8): the builder offers kinded types by name. Per decision 749 + ruling 1\nthe type's name stays its parent and the sub-sort rides as its kind: `set %n% = \"1.5\" as\ndecimal` lands %n% as `{number, kind: decimal}`. Today's name assert is green already\n(baseline: number 5/5), so the kind.name assert is the red one.",
